    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "2026-04-07",
      "text": "2026-04-07",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        632.0,
        645.0,
        649.0,
        685.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "News article text",
      "text": "The kea package has moved all services to run as a dedicated kea user (instead of root) for improved security. This change requires permission updates to the runtime files created by the kea services.",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        653.0,
        20.0,
        720.0,
        683.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "News article text",
      "text": "Users upgrading from an existing kea installation should therefore run the following commands after the upgrade:",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        721.0,
        21.0,
        757.0,
        676.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "command snippet",
      "text": "chown kea: /var/lib/kea/* /var/log/kea/* /run/lock/kea/logger_lockfile",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        757.0,
        27.0,
        784.0,
        670.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "command snippet",
      "text": "systemctl try-restart kea-ctrl-agent.service kea-dhcp{4,6}-ddns}.service",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        787.0,
        27.0,
        815.0,
        678.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "News article text",
      "text": "Accounts that need to interact with kea services files (e.g. lease files under /var/lib/kea, log files under /var/log/kea or configuration files under /etc/kea) should be added to the kea group.",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        816.0,
        23.0,
        860.0,
        681.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "link",
      "label": "iptables now defaults to the nft backend",
      "text": "iptables now defaults to the nft backend",
      "actionable": true,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        860.0,
        19.0,
        883.0,
        374.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "2026-04-05",
      "text": "2026-04-05",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        861.0,
        645.0,
        878.0,
        685.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "News article text",
      "text": "The old iptables-nft package name is replaced by iptables, and the legacy backend is available as iptables-legacy.",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        884.0,
        20.0,
        925.0,
        684.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "News article text",
      "text": "When switching packages (among iptables-nft, iptables, iptables-legacy), check for .pacsave files in /etc/iptables/ and restore your rules if needed:",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        927.0,
        21.0,
        968.0,
        680.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "command list item",
      "text": "/etc/iptables/iptables.rules.pacsave",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        969.0,
        37.0,
        979.0,
        247.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "command list item",
      "text": "/etc/iptables/ip6tables.rules.pacsave",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        969.0,
        36.0,
        979.0,
        247.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "label": "News article text",
      "text": "Most setups should work unchanged, but users relying on uncommon xtables extensions or legacy-only behavior should test carefully and use iptables-legacy if required.",
      "actionable": false,
      "is_feedback": false,
      "bbox": [
        970.0,
        20.0,
        1000.0,
        684.0
      ]
    },
